WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.612
Many organizations keep their people in Microsoft Entra ID, also known as Azure Active Directory.

00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:10.863
The Microsoft Entra ID feature lets those people sign in to your Orchard

00:00:10.863 --> 00:00:12.715
Core site with that account.

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:15.930
Let's connect the two and look at the sign-in button.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:25.297
With this feature, people enter their credentials at Microsoft, not on your site.

00:00:25.297 --> 00:00:29.352
The login page shows a button, and selecting it sends the browser to

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:31.160
the Microsoft sign-in page.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:37.235
Microsoft then sends the browser back to a path on your site, the callback path.

00:00:37.235 --> 00:00:42.250
From what Microsoft reports, Orchard Core decides which user the person is.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.048
In the Azure portal, open App registrations and select New registration.

00:00:51.048 --> 00:00:55.115
Name the app, choose the account types, and add a redirect URI:

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:58.710
the address of your site followed by the callback path.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.742
When the app exists, the portal shows two values that Orchard Core needs:

00:01:04.742 --> 00:01:09.020
the Application (client) ID and the Directory (tenant) ID.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.090
Copy both.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.940
Under Authentication, in the section for implicit grant and hybrid flows, enable Access

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.711
tokens and ID tokens.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.860
The reference documentation asks for both.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:28.652
Under Token configuration, select Add optional claim, choose the ID token type, and

00:01:28.652 --> 00:01:30.418
add the email claim.

00:01:30.418 --> 00:01:36.460
Without it, Orchard Core cannot match a login to an existing user by email address.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.984
The audience you choose in the portal and the tenant ID you enter

00:01:44.984 --> 00:01:47.055
in Orchard Core go together.

00:01:47.055 --> 00:01:52.780
The Directory (tenant) ID of your own directory allows only its user and guest accounts.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:59.553
The word organizations allows work or school accounts from any Microsoft Entra directory.

00:01:59.553 --> 00:02:03.040
The word common adds personal Microsoft accounts.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.590
Both widen the audience, so choose them with care.

00:02:10.811 --> 00:02:15.231
In the admin, open Tools, Features, and search for Entra ID.

00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:23.871
The feature is called Microsoft Entra ID (Azure Active Directory) Authentication, in the Microsoft Authentication category.

00:02:24.322 --> 00:02:25.436
Select Enable.

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:30.616
Orchard Core also enables External Authentication, which this feature depends on, and a

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:33.512
message confirms that the feature was enabled.

00:02:37.716 --> 00:02:42.154
Open Settings, Security, Authentication, Microsoft Entra ID.

00:02:42.154 --> 00:02:49.886
A notice warns that the website might be restarted upon saving the settings, with temporary unresponsiveness.

00:02:50.343 --> 00:02:53.226
Display Name is the text of the sign-in button.

00:02:53.226 --> 00:02:58.068
A name that mentions your organization and Microsoft, such as Maple Works Microsoft

00:02:58.068 --> 00:03:00.733
account, tells people which account to use.

00:03:01.196 --> 00:03:07.350
AppId takes the Application (client) ID, and TenantId takes the Directory (tenant) ID,

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.558
both from the Azure portal.

00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:12.701
The values in this recording are made up.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:16.246
These two fields and Display Name are required.

00:03:16.723 --> 00:03:18.484
CallbackPath is optional.

00:03:18.484 --> 00:03:22.291
Leave it empty to use the default path shown in the field, or

00:03:22.291 --> 00:03:24.791
enter a path that starts with a slash.

00:03:24.791 --> 00:03:28.313
It must match the redirect URI registered in the portal.

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:33.033
Store tokens keeps the external authentication tokens for reuse.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:35.821
It is optional, and we leave it cleared.

00:03:36.287 --> 00:03:37.430
Select Save.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:44.347
The message Site settings updated successfully appears, and the site may restart to apply the settings.

00:03:48.647 --> 00:03:51.656
Signed out, the login page shows two sections.

00:03:51.656 --> 00:03:54.145
The local Log in form is on the left.

00:03:54.145 --> 00:03:58.079
On the right, Use another service to log in has a button named

00:03:58.079 --> 00:03:59.757
after the Display Name.

00:04:00.235 --> 00:04:05.565
The button appears only when the feature is enabled and Display Name, AppId

00:04:05.565 --> 00:04:07.605
and TenantId are all set.

00:04:08.065 --> 00:04:12.179
Selecting the button sends the browser to Microsoft to sign in.

00:04:12.179 --> 00:04:17.665
We stop here, because completing the sign-in needs a real account in a real directory.

00:04:21.865 --> 00:04:26.319
When Microsoft sends the person back, Orchard Core first looks for a user

00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:28.969
already linked to that Microsoft account.

00:04:28.969 --> 00:04:32.521
If there is one, the person is signed in as that user, as

00:04:32.521 --> 00:04:35.115
long as that user is allowed to sign in.

00:04:35.865 --> 00:04:39.446
If no user is linked, Orchard Core looks for a user with the

00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:41.779
email address that Microsoft reports.

00:04:41.779 --> 00:04:46.663
The person sees Link your account, enters that account's local password, and selects

00:04:46.663 --> 00:04:48.345
Register to link the two.

00:04:49.095 --> 00:04:53.558
If no user matches, a local account is created, with the details the

00:04:53.558 --> 00:04:56.273
external registration settings ask for.

00:04:56.273 --> 00:05:01.400
If those settings disable new registrations, the person sees a message that New

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.235
registrations are disabled for this site.

00:05:04.985 --> 00:05:08.034
Existing users can also link their account later.

00:05:08.034 --> 00:05:12.469
When an external provider is enabled, the user menu has an External Logins

00:05:12.469 --> 00:05:15.685
page, where they add another service to log in with.

00:05:16.435 --> 00:05:21.582
Options that apply to every external provider live in two places, User Login

00:05:21.582 --> 00:05:24.658
and Registration, under Settings, Security.

00:05:24.658 --> 00:05:26.855
A separate video covers them.

00:05:31.055 --> 00:05:34.949
The Orchard Core guide for Microsoft Entra ID adds roles.

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:39.461
You create a security group in Entra ID for each Orchard Core role,

00:05:39.461 --> 00:05:44.715
and in the app registration you add the groups claim under Token configuration.

00:05:45.465 --> 00:05:49.414
In Orchard Core, the User Login option Use a script to set user

00:05:49.414 --> 00:05:54.279
roles, user claims and user properties based on external provider claims runs a

00:05:54.279 --> 00:05:57.027
script that can map those groups to roles.

00:05:57.027 --> 00:06:00.175
The guide on docs.orchardcore.net has the script.

00:06:02.175 --> 00:06:07.002
Microsoft Entra ID sign-in connects an app registration in Azure to the login

00:06:07.002 --> 00:06:08.398
page of your site.

00:06:08.398 --> 00:06:13.283
Register the app, enable the feature, enter the AppId and TenantId, and people

00:06:13.283 --> 00:06:15.493
sign in with their work account.

00:06:15.493 --> 00:06:17.005
Thanks for watching.

